     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I am trying to generate a plot in which I can control the position of geom_jitter or geom_points on the x-axis according to two different variables.</div><div>The data are plots according to the x-axis variable that has three levels.</div><div>The position of the points should also respect the differentiation determined by the factor variable that has two levels.</div><div>As a result each level of the first variable should have two distinguished groups of points.</div><div>I can do it using geom_boxplot obtaing 6 boxplots, but I do not know how to plot the overlapping points on the two different boxplots for each level of the x-axis variable.</div><div><br></div><div>Here is my code.</div><div><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px\"><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" style=\"font:normal normal normal 11px/normal Monaco\">p</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" color=\"#001f93\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco;color:#001f93\"> = </font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco\">qplot</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" color=\"#001f93\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco;color:#001f93\">(</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco\">factor</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" color=\"#001f93\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco;color:#001f93\"> (</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" style=\"font:normal normal normal 11px/normal Monaco\">x</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" color=\"#001f93\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco;color:#001f93\">), </font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" style=\"font:normal normal normal 11px/normal Monaco\">y</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" color=\"#001f93\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco;color:#001f93\">, </font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco\">colour</font><font face=\"Monaco\" size=\"3\" color=\"#001f93\" style=\"font:11.0px Monaco;color:#001f93\"> = </font><font fa